Package: SyntenyViz
Title: Visualise the synteny of a gene structure across species
Version: 0.9.1
Author: Robert QIAO <robert.qiao@flinders.edu.au> [aut, cre] (<https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4569-6921>)
Maintainer: Robert QIAO <robert.qiao@flinders.edu.au>
Authors@R: person(given = "Robert", family = "QIAO", email = "robert.qiao@flinders.edu.au",
                  comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-4569-6921"),
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: SyntenyViz provides quick and easy visualization of synteny across various species with transcriptomics evidence.
  Synteny refers to the preserved order of genes on chromosomes between related species and is a strong indicator of evolutionary conservation.
  This package enables intuitive examination of synteny patterns and facilitates reconstruction of ancestral genomes through phylogeny.
